WEBVTT

00:10.390 --> 00:11.370
Ouch.

00:15.700 --> 00:20.060
Can I really get to school in this blizzard?

00:20.060 --> 00:23.350
Especially with my muscles so 
sore from skiing yesterday.

00:24.000 --> 00:26.420
The land of Hokkaido will test your resolve.

00:26.710 --> 00:27.590
Huh?

00:28.320 --> 00:32.600
You must endure the blizzard 
to become a true citizen!

00:33.190 --> 00:34.540
Grandma...

00:35.760 --> 00:37.520
I'll do my best!

00:38.240 --> 00:39.330
See you later!

01:03.250 --> 01:05.910
<i>No way, no way, no way!</i>

01:07.990 --> 01:09.170
<i>It's just too cold!</i>

01:09.730 --> 01:11.680
<i>My muscles are so sore!</i>

01:11.880 --> 01:14.440
<i>The snow is stabbing my face! It hurts!</i>

01:15.880 --> 01:18.760
<i>It's more than cold. It's piercing!</i>

01:19.910 --> 01:23.190
<i>Everything is white and I can't see ahead!</i>

01:23.430 --> 01:25.540
<i>I can even walk right.</i>

01:25.540 --> 01:27.690
<i>I'm practically trapped!</i>

01:33.110 --> 01:39.160
<i>I bet Fuyuki-san walks to school like 
normal, even on days like these.</i>

01:49.510 --> 01:50.480
<i>Okay.</i>

01:51.910 --> 01:53.270
Whoa! I'm sorry!

01:57.280 --> 01:58.560
I'm gonna die.

02:04.580 --> 02:07.400
<i>Right. Life flashes before your eyes.</i>

02:09.060 --> 02:11.210
<i>Farewell, Hokkaido.</i>

02:12.050 --> 02:14.470
<i>Farewell, my life!</i>

02:14.470 --> 02:16.410
What the heck are you doin'?!

02:16.670 --> 02:19.910
You can't walk around in 
a blizzard! That's wack!

02:20.140 --> 02:22.120
Get in the car with me.

02:22.640 --> 02:26.350
Sure. Is this... the afterlife?

02:26.350 --> 02:28.710
Just hurry up and get in!

02:45.180 --> 02:47.850
<b>Hokkaido Gals Are Super Adorable!</b>

02:48.690 --> 02:52.060
<b>Hokkaido Gals Are Super Adorable!</b>

04:00.220 --> 04:02.970
Super Cute Angels ♥

04:00.220 --> 04:02.970
<b>Hokkaido Gals Are</b>

04:00.220 --> 04:02.970
<b>Boom!</b>

04:00.220 --> 04:02.970
<b>Super Adorable</b>

04:03.840 --> 04:08.310
<b>Episode 4:
Nighttime Calls Are Super Ticklish</b>

04:03.840 --> 04:08.310
<b>Episode 4:
Nighttime Calls Are Super Ticklish</b>

04:06.450 --> 04:11.530
G-Good morning.
I'm sorry to trouble you.

04:11.530 --> 04:14.020
Mom, you can get rolling now.

04:14.560 --> 04:16.040
Okey-dokey!

04:16.890 --> 04:22.830
It's really freezing today. 
Just relax and make yourself at home.

04:23.140 --> 04:24.270
<i>Another gyaru!</i>

04:25.120 --> 04:27.580
<i>And it's... her mother?</i>

04:27.580 --> 04:29.670
<i>Not sister, but mother?!</i>

04:29.970 --> 04:32.380
<i>She looks exactly like Fuyuki-san!</i>

04:32.380 --> 04:34.740
<i>Now that's a strong bloodline!</i>

04:35.090 --> 04:40.410
Tsubasa lives in a mansion, so I bet 
our car is way too cramped for him.

04:40.410 --> 04:42.250
No, that isn't true.

04:42.250 --> 04:47.660
Huh? Is this the rich kid in the castle 
that you keep talking about, Mii?

04:47.660 --> 04:49.690
R-Rich kid?

04:49.690 --> 04:54.320
Aww! If I'd known, 
I would've gotten all made up first.

04:54.320 --> 04:57.250
Come on, Mom! Quit trying to up-pick Tsubasa!

04:57.250 --> 04:58.320
Up-pick?

04:58.320 --> 05:03.680
All right, all right! So you are the 
Tsubasa I keep hearing about. Huh...

05:03.680 --> 05:05.760
<i>Why does this make me feel so anxious?</i>

05:05.760 --> 05:09.200
So, Tsubasa-kun, do you have 
a girlfriend back home?

05:09.200 --> 05:09.660
Gir—!?

05:09.910 --> 05:12.100
Why are you overreacting?

05:12.100 --> 05:14.290
Ow, ow, ow!

05:12.850 --> 05:16.320
Huh? Oh, sorry! Are you okay?

05:16.640 --> 05:19.880
Yeah, I'm just sore.

05:20.590 --> 05:24.800
I used a lot of muscles in ski 
class that I usually don't.

05:24.800 --> 05:26.390
Oh, dear.

05:26.800 --> 05:29.270
M'kay, I guess that means...

05:29.750 --> 05:32.900
I guess I shouldn't get too 
rough with you, Tsubasa.

05:33.250 --> 05:35.040
<i>Don't say it like that!</i>

05:36.320 --> 05:38.690
You've def got the stamina though, Mii.

05:38.690 --> 05:41.240
You could pound at it all 
day long without a break.

05:41.840 --> 05:43.610
<i>Mom sounds like trouble, too.</i>

05:44.500 --> 05:46.380
You seem all right, Fuyuki-san.

05:46.380 --> 05:48.330
Yeah, I'm totally fine.

05:48.330 --> 05:50.080
O-Oh, okay.

05:51.880 --> 05:55.910
Um... Well, no, I don't have a girlfriend.

05:55.910 --> 05:58.060
Aw, what a waste!

05:58.060 --> 05:58.750
It's okay.

05:58.750 --> 06:00.860
<i>What does she mean a waste?!</i>

06:00.860 --> 06:03.180
How about my Mii, then? Isn't she adorable?

06:03.180 --> 06:07.050
Jeez, Mom! You're embarrassing 
me! Seriously, cut it out!

06:07.050 --> 06:11.560
<i>This is just like the first 
time I met Fuyuki-san.</i>

06:11.760 --> 06:15.900
But isn't Tsubasa-kun adorable? 
He looks just like your papa!

06:15.900 --> 06:18.570
Your Mama hasn't felt this 
tingly in a long time!

06:18.570 --> 06:23.080
Mii and Tsuba-chi, like a bee and honey! 
You'd make such an adorable couple!

06:23.080 --> 06:27.090
<i>She's getting so carried away, 
I don't know how to respond!</i>

06:27.090 --> 06:28.120
Mom...

06:33.840 --> 06:37.060
Uh... Hey now, you don't 
need to get that angry.

06:37.060 --> 06:40.080
I'm just happy to meet Tsuba-chi! 
I guess I got a little excited.

06:40.080 --> 06:40.810
Hmph!

06:41.440 --> 06:44.610
<i>So this is how Fuyuki-san 
acts when she's angry.</i>

06:44.610 --> 06:47.340
<i>She isn't scary at all, 
but I'd better be careful regardless.</i>

06:53.850 --> 06:56.500
Tsuba-chi, you're from Tokyo, right?

06:56.500 --> 06:58.400
I bet you've never seen a 
blizzard like this before.

06:58.620 --> 07:01.810
I honestly don't understand 
why school isn't closed today.

07:01.810 --> 07:03.510
I know, right?

07:03.510 --> 07:07.570
But actually, this isn't nearly 
enough for that to happen.

07:08.010 --> 07:10.900
If it snowed this much in Tokyo,

07:10.900 --> 07:13.730
I think people would act like 
it was the end of the world.

07:13.730 --> 07:17.580
Yeah, it would probably be on the news. 
But this is normal here.

07:18.000 --> 07:21.710
I bet it doesn't seem normal 
when you're from Tokyo.

07:21.710 --> 07:23.830
One thing does surprise me, though.

07:23.830 --> 07:24.690
Hmm?

07:25.150 --> 07:27.570
The locals here are so used to the cold,

07:27.570 --> 07:30.550
I thought they'd be out and 
about even in weather like this.

07:30.550 --> 07:32.390
Not a chance!

07:38.350 --> 07:41.090
Most kids who don't take the 
bus or train to school

07:41.090 --> 07:43.850
get their parents or 
someone to drop them off.

07:43.850 --> 07:45.700
Oh, really?

07:45.700 --> 07:47.490
Yeah, especially in winter.

07:48.040 --> 07:51.290
I want to look good, 
so I usually dress light.

07:51.290 --> 07:54.500
But it gets straight-up cold in winter, 
so I don't want to go outside.

07:54.500 --> 07:56.470
Really?

07:56.470 --> 08:01.250
So when Grandma said "true citizen of 
Hokkaido," what did she actually mean?

08:01.540 --> 08:06.990
But dressing for winter is way expensive, 
so your wallet might freeze to death first.

08:07.300 --> 08:12.430
Boots and coats and stuff. And the winter 
is long, so clothing expenses are crazy.

08:12.430 --> 08:17.120
I can't afford any of the clothes I want 
on my allowance, so I want to get a job!

08:17.120 --> 08:18.980
You're too young for a job, Mii.

08:18.980 --> 08:20.760
Huh? Why though?

08:20.760 --> 08:22.690
Papa says so, too.

08:23.220 --> 08:25.490
<i>They seem like a close-knit family.</i>

08:25.910 --> 08:29.770
<i>But it must be tough being a 
gyaru in Hokkaido. Still...</i>

08:29.770 --> 08:33.530
You're both beautiful enough 
just the way you are now.

08:42.540 --> 08:46.690
Tsu... Tsuba-chi! 
Flattery will get you nowhere!

08:46.690 --> 08:50.630
Seriously, Tsubasa. 
Sometimes he says stuff like that.

08:50.630 --> 08:53.630
<i>Oh, crap! I said it out loud again!</i>

08:57.910 --> 08:59.600
We're here.

08:59.860 --> 09:03.380
Thank you very much. 
You really saved me out there.

09:04.330 --> 09:07.030
Isn't your house close to ours, Tsuba-chi?

09:07.030 --> 09:10.070
Yes. It's about a ten minute walk.

09:10.340 --> 09:14.500
M'kay. Then next time a blizzard 
comes, I'll give you a ride.

09:14.500 --> 09:17.000
Is that all right? That would really help!

09:17.000 --> 09:20.550
All good, all good. Just let Mii know.

09:20.550 --> 09:23.500
All right. Thank you very much!

09:26.000 --> 09:26.740
Ow!

09:28.560 --> 09:30.370
Laters!

09:30.370 --> 09:32.930
Ah, yes! See you later.

09:34.280 --> 09:35.250
Mii.

09:35.250 --> 09:36.180
What?

09:36.740 --> 09:40.270
That was one fine play you made back there.

09:44.100 --> 09:45.720
Just a little one, I guess.

09:46.780 --> 09:48.050
Bye-bye!

09:50.460 --> 09:53.560
Tsubasa! Let's run to class for shelter!

09:53.560 --> 09:58.360
Ow! There's snow in my eye! 
My muscles hurt so much!

09:58.360 --> 10:03.620
Even during a blizzardy winter, 
it's still springtime for some.

10:15.630 --> 10:17.880
Are you okay? Want a hand?

10:17.880 --> 10:20.040
No, I'm fine.

10:21.210 --> 10:22.390
It's Akino-san.

10:24.810 --> 10:26.480
Sayuri-chan!

10:26.880 --> 10:28.790
Morning!

10:27.330 --> 10:28.790
Wait—!

10:33.880 --> 10:36.830
Fuyuki... I'll never forgive you for that.

10:36.830 --> 10:39.490
Huh? What's wrong, Sayuri-chan?

10:39.910 --> 10:42.810
Are your muscles sore, too, Akino-san?

10:43.400 --> 10:44.290
You, too, Shiki?

10:44.950 --> 10:47.360
Pretty much all over.

10:47.360 --> 10:49.090
I totally get you!

10:49.090 --> 10:52.890
That was way too much for beginners like us.

10:53.560 --> 10:55.110
Definitely.

10:55.110 --> 10:59.920
Not fair! 
Quit acting so friendly without me!

10:59.920 --> 11:04.160
We're not acting <i>that</i> friendly, though. 
Right, Shiki?

11:04.160 --> 11:08.950
Uh, yeah. Not super friendly, at least.

11:10.720 --> 11:14.860
Now I wanna get sore muscles, too!

11:22.030 --> 11:25.710
So, Tsubasa, it looks like you finally 
got a cardigan and blanket and stuff.

11:25.710 --> 11:29.620
Yeah. It's tough to live 
in Hokkaido without them,

11:29.620 --> 11:32.800
and I felt bad borrowing 
from you all the time.

11:32.800 --> 11:36.250
Huh? You didn't need to worry about that.

11:37.170 --> 11:39.730
M'kay, but how about these?

11:40.750 --> 11:41.810
Got warmers with you?

11:47.360 --> 11:49.090
I didn't bring any.

11:50.560 --> 11:54.280
<i>I caught a glimpse of why 
Fuyuki-san can dress so light!</i>

11:54.640 --> 11:57.940
I'll lend you some, then. 
Feel free to use them.

11:57.940 --> 12:00.280
The cold weather in Kitami is no joke!

12:00.280 --> 12:02.530
Oh. Thank you.

12:06.240 --> 12:08.560
This is such a strange feeling, though.

12:09.710 --> 12:14.210
I never imagined myself getting along 
so well with a gyaru like Fuyuki-san.

12:15.280 --> 12:18.630
This would have been unthinkable 
back when I was in Tokyo.

12:19.450 --> 12:22.060
I need to get some new lipstick soon.

12:22.060 --> 12:24.100
M'kay, so why not buy one after class?

12:24.100 --> 12:24.880
Oh!

12:24.880 --> 12:25.430
Huh?

12:25.790 --> 12:30.380
You just said "m'kay"! 
You're using Hokkaido dialect!

12:32.000 --> 12:34.080
Huh? Oh. You're right.

12:34.080 --> 12:38.030
I bet you picked it up from me! 
That kinda makes me happy.

12:38.030 --> 12:40.860
Now you're a Hokkaido local 
just like us, Tsuba-cha.

12:41.250 --> 12:45.110
Oh, yeah? A Hokkaido local...

12:46.210 --> 12:47.040
Shiki.

12:50.110 --> 12:52.860
You shouldn't count on Fuyuki as an example.

12:52.860 --> 12:53.540
Huh?

12:54.030 --> 12:56.260
You must have noticed, right?

12:56.260 --> 12:59.080
How exceptional Fuyuki is, in a lot of ways.

13:01.970 --> 13:06.040
What are you talking about? 
I'm pure Hokkaido, born and raised!

13:06.040 --> 13:07.930
Well, so am I!

13:08.300 --> 13:12.690
But I don't use a lot of the local dialect 
and I don't have much of an accent.

13:13.010 --> 13:19.370
I'm not very good at skiing or winter sports. 
And there are a lot of locals like me.

13:20.480 --> 13:25.030
<i>Akino-san never speaks up like that. 
It looks like it deflated her.</i>

13:25.280 --> 13:30.070
But my family and relatives in 
Sapporo all use Hokkaido dialect.

13:30.070 --> 13:32.490
Most of my relatives don't.

13:32.490 --> 13:35.130
It's basically just my 
grandpa and grandma that do.

13:36.410 --> 13:41.450
It's probably different depending 
on location, family, and age.

13:42.890 --> 13:44.390
Akino-san, is that...

13:44.390 --> 13:47.820
Oh! You noticed? 
Yeah, I thought I might as well bring it.

13:47.820 --> 13:51.510
But if you aren't really into it, 
we don't have to do it.

13:51.510 --> 13:53.400
Huh? Of course I do!

13:53.400 --> 13:56.070
I want to do it with you, Akino-san!

14:00.940 --> 14:02.750
Shiki, you're too innocent!

14:03.160 --> 14:07.110
Akino-san is my professor now. 
Do you want to become a pupil, too?

14:07.110 --> 14:10.720
I do, I do! I don't know what 
she's a professor of, but I'm in!

14:10.720 --> 14:12.460
Hear that, Professor?

14:14.860 --> 14:16.930
So can I join you guys?

14:20.390 --> 14:21.510
Yeah, sure.

14:21.900 --> 14:24.240
Let's meet at Tobu after class, then.

14:24.240 --> 14:26.890
All right! I'm super excited!

14:26.890 --> 14:27.930
Tobu?

14:35.200 --> 14:39.860
That's the fashion section 
and here's the food court.

14:40.100 --> 14:42.690
And there's a grocery 
store with tons of meat!

14:42.690 --> 14:46.490
Huh... This place is huge.

14:46.490 --> 14:48.740
Aren't the stores in Tokyo fancier, though?

14:48.960 --> 14:54.040
Yeah, but this seems a little different 
from your average shopping mall.

14:54.040 --> 14:55.670
Oh? What's different?

14:55.670 --> 14:57.280
This is more spacious.

14:57.280 --> 14:59.430
Well, yeah. There's a lot of land.

15:00.400 --> 15:04.410
The atmosphere isn't as busy, 
so you can kind of relax.

15:05.080 --> 15:06.270
You think so?

15:06.270 --> 15:07.480
Sounds like it.

15:08.640 --> 15:10.420
Ah! Stop! No!

15:10.420 --> 15:11.810
A little more! Run!

15:11.810 --> 15:13.470
Left, left! Ah, watch out!

15:13.470 --> 15:15.470
Yes! Right there! Grenade!

15:24.610 --> 15:26.760
Yay!

15:26.760 --> 15:27.740
Yay!

15:30.950 --> 15:32.870
I need the bathroom.

15:32.870 --> 15:35.240
That way and then turn left.

15:35.240 --> 15:36.500
We'll be here.

15:39.030 --> 15:39.920
Hey, hey, hey!

15:39.920 --> 15:41.380
What now?

15:41.380 --> 15:44.120
Wanna check cosmetics on the way out?

15:44.120 --> 15:45.720
I know you love that stuff, Sayurin!

15:46.040 --> 15:47.680
S-Sayurin?!

15:47.680 --> 15:49.930
Yeah! Sayuri, so Sayurin, right?

15:50.220 --> 15:51.640
Wanna go? Let's go!

15:53.080 --> 15:53.990
Mm-hmm.

15:54.930 --> 15:58.320
Color contacts are expensive, 
so maybe we can buy some together.

15:58.320 --> 16:01.730
Oh, nice! We can share them!

16:01.730 --> 16:06.500
I also want to get lipstick 
and buy some shampoo.

16:07.770 --> 16:08.990
Fuyuki, you know,

16:10.530 --> 16:12.150
you're actually a real nice gal.

16:16.930 --> 16:20.030
Sorry I act so grouchy to you at school.

16:20.030 --> 16:23.990
It's okay! It never even bothered me.

16:23.990 --> 16:26.130
Oh, he's back.

16:31.050 --> 16:33.050
<b>ular Cosmetics</b>

16:31.050 --> 16:33.050
<b>Make Up Accessories</b>

16:31.050 --> 16:33.050
Bathroom Supplies         Shampoo

16:37.560 --> 16:40.060
<b>Popular Cos</b>

16:42.700 --> 16:45.480
I bought the shampoo that Tsubasa picked!

16:45.480 --> 16:46.370
Huh?

16:46.370 --> 16:48.930
Got the contacts Shiki approved, too.

16:48.930 --> 16:51.320
Ah... Sorry in advance 
if they don't look right!

16:52.920 --> 16:54.370
All good!

16:54.370 --> 16:56.160
Ah, we synced!

16:56.160 --> 16:57.800
I love it!

16:59.300 --> 17:02.130
Uh, we'd better start heading home.

17:02.630 --> 17:03.790
I guess you're right.

17:05.360 --> 17:06.720
Oh, that's right!

17:06.720 --> 17:10.310
Before we go, why don't 
the three of us do that?

17:10.630 --> 17:15.880
Natural Beauty
Lovable Fair Skin

17:10.630 --> 17:15.880
Cute
8 Pictures

17:10.850 --> 17:11.860
How about this one?

17:11.860 --> 17:13.270
Fine with me. But Shiki?

17:13.270 --> 17:13.940
Huh?

17:13.940 --> 17:14.840
Aww, come on.

17:14.840 --> 17:15.890
Um... okay.

17:15.890 --> 17:18.970
Let's hang out again soon ♥

17:15.890 --> 17:18.970
<b>We're All Super Adorable</b>

17:19.100 --> 17:25.900
Minami

17:19.100 --> 17:25.900
Tsuba-cha

17:19.100 --> 17:25.900
hilar lol

17:19.100 --> 17:25.900
Sayurin

17:42.400 --> 17:46.920
Wait. Is English homework due in class?

17:48.000 --> 17:50.010
Fuyuki-san probably knows.

17:52.430 --> 17:52.980
Do we turn English homework
in during class?
Not sure what I'm supposed
to do.

17:53.880 --> 17:57.880
Minami

17:53.880 --> 17:57.880
Tsuba-cha

17:53.880 --> 17:57.880
hilar lol

17:53.880 --> 17:57.880
Sayurin

18:01.150 --> 18:03.190
Fuyuki-san? That was fast!

18:03.190 --> 18:04.940
Taking a half bath

18:03.190 --> 18:04.940
<b>Taking a half bath!</b>

18:06.640 --> 18:11.130
S-Sorry. When you get out, 
could you tell me—

18:11.930 --> 18:12.490
Huh?

18:12.490 --> 18:14.490
Just like this

18:14.760 --> 18:18.240
Well then, how is Tsubasa gonna react?

18:18.660 --> 18:20.290
I bet he'll freak out!

18:20.760 --> 18:21.430
Oh.

18:21.430 --> 18:25.910
<b>Sorry I caught you in the bath. 
That's a cute fox toy!</b>

18:33.160 --> 18:34.730
<i>What the hell?!</i>

18:35.790 --> 18:39.890
<i>There's no way I can concentrate on 
homework after seeing something like that!</i>

18:40.160 --> 18:45.030
I might have overdone it a little, 
but now I know I'll get a good reaction.

18:45.520 --> 18:46.530
Yes!

18:46.530 --> 18:49.200
<b>Wow, you truly are serious 
about your beauty routine.</b>

18:49.200 --> 18:51.580
<b>With all the effort you 
put into this one picture,</b>

18:51.580 --> 18:55.190
<b>your devotion becomes crystal clear!</b>

18:57.410 --> 18:59.930
<i>Was that the right response?</i>

19:01.180 --> 19:01.830
Huh?

19:01.830 --> 19:04.080
Fuyuki-san
Incoming Call

19:02.330 --> 19:04.080
Huh? She's calling?!

19:04.320 --> 19:06.210
<i>Sh-Should I answer?</i>

19:10.990 --> 19:12.050
Hello?

19:12.550 --> 19:15.550
<i>My more rational option, 
to ignore it, was found killed in action.</i>

19:15.550 --> 19:17.340
<i>Are you seeing this?</i>

19:19.010 --> 19:20.430
<i>Hey.</i>

19:21.460 --> 19:24.020
<i>Fuyuki-san!
Th-The bu— You're in the bath?!</i>

19:24.020 --> 19:25.540
<i>You can't do a video call there!</i>

19:25.540 --> 19:27.900
Now <i>that's</i> the reaction I was expecting.

19:28.320 --> 19:30.360
<i>Your face is bright red.</i>

19:30.360 --> 19:32.650
Huh?! It's showing me...

19:33.000 --> 19:33.840
<i>It isn't?</i>

19:35.250 --> 19:36.650
Totally hilarious!

19:36.650 --> 19:38.560
This is fun!

19:40.610 --> 19:42.950
<i>She's hitting harder than usual!</i>

19:44.360 --> 19:47.000
<i>Any more of this and I have 
reason to fear for my life.</i>

19:48.010 --> 19:51.380
Hey, hey, Tsubasa. 
Do you soak in the bath every day?

19:51.670 --> 19:54.710
Yeah, I soak. I got out a little while ago.

19:54.710 --> 19:58.600
Yeah? Other than me and Mom, 
everyone here goes every other day.

19:58.600 --> 20:00.660
They shower every day, though.

20:00.660 --> 20:05.280
Really? Since it's so cold, I figured 
you'd soak in the tub every day.

20:05.280 --> 20:09.510
I guess my dad doesn't sweat much, 
and the power bills would be insane,

20:09.510 --> 20:11.600
so he said going every day is cray-cray.

20:11.600 --> 20:16.140
But if you and your mom take a bath every 
day, doesn't that defeat the purpose?

20:16.140 --> 20:18.770
Half baths aren't nearly as bad, though.

20:18.770 --> 20:21.480
Budgeting utilities in the 
winter must be tricky.

20:21.480 --> 20:25.790
Now that I think of it, our family used 
to go on hot spring trips all the time.

20:25.790 --> 20:27.300
Hot springs sound nice!

20:27.300 --> 20:29.920
There are a bunch of them in Kitami, 
so you should try some out.

20:29.920 --> 20:31.920
Yeah! I'll check them out.

20:31.920 --> 20:34.780
Or would you rather go together, with me?

20:37.000 --> 20:40.550
Okay, you're not going to rattle 
me this time, Fuyuki-san.

20:40.550 --> 20:43.470
Aww, you're no fun!

20:44.060 --> 20:46.790
Anyway, what are you doing now, Tsuba-cha?

20:46.790 --> 20:50.140
English homework. 
I was doing today's assignment.

20:50.140 --> 20:54.340
<i>Oh, right. We have to turn 
this in tomorrow, don't we?</i>

20:54.340 --> 20:55.900
<i>I wanted to ask about that...</i>

20:55.900 --> 21:00.190
Oh, crap! I haven't even 
started the first page ye—

21:00.190 --> 21:01.200
Fuyuki-san? Ah!

21:21.300 --> 21:23.640
What happened, Fuyuki-san? Are you okay?

21:23.630 --> 21:25.510
Fuyuki-san
In Call

21:24.380 --> 21:25.510
Fuyuki-san?

21:26.950 --> 21:27.940
<i>Did you see?</i>

21:29.240 --> 21:30.500
<i>Huh? See what?</i>

21:30.500 --> 21:31.720
Just now.

21:31.720 --> 21:34.880
Sorry, no. I was surprised 
and almost dropped my phone.

21:37.190 --> 21:41.200
<i>Okay. I have to get out 
so I should probably go.</i>

21:41.200 --> 21:42.280
Ah, sure.

21:42.660 --> 21:44.320
See you tomorrow, then.

21:47.530 --> 21:50.200
What's up with Fuyuki-san?

21:50.660 --> 21:53.810
Was the homework that much of a shock to her?

22:01.570 --> 22:04.550
I shouldn't try things I'm not used to.

22:06.240 --> 22:07.760
Mii, you out?

22:08.220 --> 22:10.560
I want to get in the bath.

22:10.560 --> 22:12.560
What's wrong? Feeling lightheaded?

22:12.970 --> 22:14.560
No. Well...

22:15.750 --> 22:18.700
maybe a little bit.

22:22.750 --> 22:24.130
<i>The next day,</i>

22:24.130 --> 22:28.970
<i>Fuyuki-san didn't turn her homework in on time, 
so she got in trouble with the teacher.</i>
